From: Raven maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] serial: avoid empty-read retry spin in asynchronous mode

VMIN=0 permits successful zero-byte reads from an empty tty. Asio maps
those reads to EOF, which the receive handler immediately re-arms. On
the i.MX95 RPMsg tty this consumes a CPU core while idle. Require one
byte for tty readiness; Asio retains O_NONBLOCK and handles EAGAIN.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/cpp/src/mavsdk/core/serial_connection.cpp
+++ b/cpp/src/mavsdk/core/serial_connection.cpp
@@ -140,8 +140,9 @@ ConnectionResult SerialConnection::setup_port()
     tc.c_cflag |= CS8;
     tc.c_cflag |= CLOCAL; // Without this a write() blocks indefinitely.
 
-    // VMIN=0 / VTIME=0: non-blocking raw mode — Asio drives readiness via epoll/kqueue.
-    tc.c_cc[VMIN] = 0;
+    // Require data for tty readiness. O_NONBLOCK still lets Asio manage I/O;
+    // VMIN=0 can repeatedly report empty reads as EOF and spin the receive loop.
+    tc.c_cc[VMIN] = 1;
     tc.c_cc[VTIME] = 0;
 
     if (_flow_control) {
